<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Großer Falkenstein via Höllbachgespreng — Heidelbeere ravine, Falkenstein and Goldsteig–Ameise return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start on Waldhausstraße at the P1 Zwieslerwaldhaus parking and Igelbus access. Follow Heidelbeere to Höllbachschwelle, turn left at the hut, then take the left stream crossing at the waterfall into the steep Höllbachgespreng ravine. Continue through the rock formations and over Höllbachriegel to Großer Falkenstein&apos;s summit walking ground and the shelter area. Descend on Goldsteig through the windthrow forest and Ruckowitzschachten pasture, then through the Mittelsteighütte old-growth forest. Turn left onto Ameise over the wooden bridge, follow the village edge to the asphalt road, and return left to the same P1 access. Approximate planning totals are 15.2 km, 700 m ascent and descent, and 5 hours 15 minutes. These are planning estimates without a surveyed elevation profile.

Plan this seasonal course for dry, snow-free daylight in summer or autumn. Relevant wildlife grounds and affected paths close from 15 November through 30 April. The ravine normally closes from 15 February through 30 April for peregrine nesting, and that closure can extend into late spring. Check the current National Park notices and on-site signs immediately before walking; marked diversions do not reproduce this full ravine variant. If the ravine is closed, this variant is unavailable. Stay on the marked adopted paths, steps and bridges. Steep wet rocks, roots, boulders and mud demand sure-footedness. Avoid the forest in strong wind because trees and deadwood can fall. Snow, ice, flooding, damage or local restrictions can prevent passage. Verify current parking, bus and shelter arrangements separately; this map does not guarantee opening or bridge conditions.

